<header class='min-h-[60vh] flex items-center justify-center text-center px-6 bg-gradient-to-br from-cyan-700 via-blue-700 to-purple-700'><div><h1 class='font-heading text-5xl md:text-7xl'>COLD SPECTRUM DOSSIER</h1><p class='max-w-3xl mt-4 text-lg'>Examining how blue-range hues modulate trust, creativity, and reduced autonomic arousal.</p></div></header>
<main class='px-6 md:px-16 py-14 space-y-12'>
<section data-aos='fade-up'><h2 class='font-heading text-3xl text-cyan-300'>Blue & Creativity</h2><p class='mt-2'>Mehta & Zhu (2009) found blue primes improved creative performance while red improved proofing/detail tasks, suggesting a goal-orientation mechanism where cool tones broaden exploration.</p><p class='text-sm opacity-80 mt-1'>Citation: Mehta, R., & Zhu, R. (2009). Blue or red? Exploring the effect of color on cognitive task performances. <em>Science</em>.</p></section>
<section data-aos='fade-up'><h2 class='font-heading text-3xl text-blue-300'>Cyan & Perceived Cleanliness</h2><p class='mt-2'>In interface studies and design practice, cyan is strongly associated with hygiene, precision, and digital transparency, making it common in med-tech and sensor dashboards.</p></section>
<section data-aos='fade-up'><h2 class='font-heading text-3xl text-purple-300'>Purple & Reflective Attention</h2><p class='mt-2'>Purple commonly communicates introspection and premium creativity. In branding tests, darker violet often increases perceived sophistication and uniqueness.</p></section>
<section><h2 class='font-heading text-3xl mb-5 text-center'>Cooling Demo Cards</h2><div class='grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-4'><div class='cool p-6 rounded-2xl bg-cyan-500/20 border border-cyan-200/30'><h3 class='font-heading'>Cool (5–15°C)</h3><p>Alert calmness and clarity.</p></div><div class='cool p-6 rounded-2xl bg-blue-500/20 border border-blue-200/30'><h3 class='font-heading'>Colder (-5–5°C)</h3><p>Control, trust, reduced urgency.</p></div><div class='cool p-6 rounded-2xl bg-purple-500/20 border border-purple-200/30'><h3 class='font-heading'>Deep Cold (-20–0°C)</h3><p>Contemplation, distance, precision focus.</p></div></div></section>
<section class='rounded-2xl border border-cyan-200/30 p-6 bg-black/30'><h3 class='font-heading text-2xl'>External Research Links</h3><ul class='list-disc pl-6 mt-3 space-y-1'><li><a class='text-cyan-300 underline' href='https://www.science.org/doi/10.1126/science.1169144' target='_blank'>Mehta & Zhu (2009)</a></li><li><a class='text-cyan-300 underline' href='https://www.annualreviews.org/doi/10.1146/annurev-psych-010213-115035' target='_blank'>Elliot & Maier (2014)</a></li><li><a class='text-cyan-300 underline' href='https://www.colorpsychology.org/' target='_blank'>colorpsychology.org</a></li></ul></section>
<section><h2 class='font-heading text-3xl mb-6 text-center'>Color Intelligence System</h2><div class='grid grid-cols-4 md:grid-cols-8 gap-3 mb-6'><template x-for='color in colors'><button @click='selected=color' class='h-16 w-16 rounded-full border border-white/40' :style='`background:${color.hex}`'></button></template></div><div x-show='selected' class='rounded-2xl border border-cyan-300/40 p-5 bg-black/35'><h3 class='font-heading text-2xl' x-text='selected.name'></h3><p><strong>Thermal Signature:</strong> <span x-text='selected.temp'></span></p><p><strong>Historical Record:</strong> <span x-text='selected.history'></span></p><p><strong>Psychological Effect:</strong> <span x-text='selected.effect'></span></p><p><strong>Real-World Applications:</strong> <span x-text='selected.use'></span></p><p><strong>Intelligence Brief:</strong> <span x-text='selected.brief'></span></p></div></section>
</main>
